+# telling it not to use them ("이런 문구는 쓰지 마: 'X', 'Y', ..."). On this
+# 7B local model that backfired hard - quoting the exact banned strings in
+# every single proactive-speak prompt acted as an anchor and made the model
+# echo them (sometimes verbatim) far more than when they weren't mentioned at
+# all. Negative instructions with literal quoted text don't reliably work on
+# a model this size; state the desired behavior positively instead, with no
+# quoted strings for it to latch onto.
+#
+# Same reasoning applies to the "don't always open with 오빠~" rule below -
+# describing the desired variety instead of naming the exact banned opener.
+PROACTIVE_SPEAK_STYLE_NOTE = (
+    "\n\n짧은 문자 보내듯 자연스럽게, 상투적이지 않은 그때그때 다른 표현으로 말해줘. "
+    "문장을 시작하는 방식도 매번 다르게 - 이름부터 부르고 시작할 때도 있고, "
+    "이름 없이 바로 용건이나 감정부터 꺼낼 때도 있게 섞어줘."
